At only 18 years old, Solomon Boss Cove left his family in Russia, emigrated to the United States in 1914.
18岁那年，所罗门·博斯·科夫离开了他在俄罗斯的家人，于1914年移民到美国。

751
00:40:55.070 --> 00:40:57.510
He settled in Redding, Pennsylvania.
他在宾夕法尼亚州的雷丁定居了下来。

752
00:40:57.810 --> 00:41:05.150
With a pack on his back and a few dollars he had, he began peddling household goods to the farm families in the surrounding area.
他背着行囊，带着仅有的几块钱，开始向周边地区的农户兜售家居用品。

753
00:41:05.370 --> 00:41:06.870
Like a door-to-door salesman?
就像上门推销员那样？

754
00:41:06.870 --> 00:41:07.570
That's right.
没错。

755
00:41:07.570 --> 00:41:11.250
And he got a reputation of being very fair and very honeSt.
他因为非常公道和诚实而赢得了良好的声誉。

756
00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:12.550
The business grew.
生意越做越大。

757
00:41:12.710 --> 00:41:13.850
His reputation grew.
他的名声也越来越响。

758
00:41:14.050 --> 00:41:17.230
He was able to buy dry goods and provide merchandise.
他开始有能力采购干货并提供各类商品。

759
00:41:17.510 --> 00:41:20.350
And the first Boss Cove's department store was established.
于是，第一家博斯·科夫百货商店就这样成立了。

760
00:41:20.670 --> 00:41:22.470
And it's still going strong today.
而且直到今天依然经营得红红火火。

761
00:41:22.910 --> 00:41:24.790
Lady, hear me out.
女士，听我说完。

762
00:41:25.010 --> 00:41:25.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

763
00:41:25.670 --> 00:41:30.950
Next time we're in Scranton, we go to Boss Cove's at the Steamtown Mall and we buy matching outfits.
下次我们去斯克兰顿时，我们就去蒸汽镇购物中心的博斯·科夫百货，买两套情侣装。

764
00:41:31.690 --> 00:41:32.010
Done!
成交！

765
00:41:32.230 --> 00:41:34.770
And then we go bowl and go to poor Richard's.
然后我们去打保龄球，再去“可怜的理查德”酒吧。

766
00:41:34.890 --> 00:41:36.470
I mean, we have a lot of places to go.
我是说，我们有很多地方可以去。

767
00:41:36.470 --> 00:41:37.730
We got a lot of places to go.
我们有很多地方可以去。

768
00:41:38.190 --> 00:41:42.150
Well, we got a lot of mail about these matching outfits.
嗯，我们收到了很多关于这些情侣装的来信。

769
00:41:42.590 --> 00:41:44.930
So many questions on how they were chosen.
大家问了很多关于这些衣服是怎么选出来的问题。

770
00:41:45.010 --> 00:41:49.810
And also, if I felt at all that this outfit was a little out of character for Pam.
还有人问我是否觉得这身装扮对帕姆来说有点不符合她的人设。

771
00:41:50.330 --> 00:41:55.710
Well, I reached out to Alicia, our wardrobe designer, for this episode.
为此，我联系了这一集的服装设计师艾丽西亚。

772
00:41:55.850 --> 00:42:00.750
And she shared with me that this storyline was a very late addition to the script.
她告诉我，这个情节是剧本后期才临时加进去的。

773
00:42:01.070 --> 00:42:05.710
She had very little time to figure out what this matching outfit will be.
她几乎没有时间去构思这套情侣装该是什么样。

774
00:42:06.290 --> 00:42:09.930
She said she normally would have made something from scratch because that's her.
她说按她平时的习惯，她会从零开始制作，因为这就是她的风格。

775
00:42:10.130 --> 00:42:14.230
I mean, this woman is amazing at building clothing.
我是说，这位女士在服装制作方面简直太厉害了。

776
00:42:14.770 --> 00:42:17.910
But because of time, she had to find existing pieces.
但由于时间紧迫，她只能去买现成的衣服。

777
00:42:17.910 --> 00:42:23.070
So Alicia started by going to the stores where she would buy Phyllis's wardrobe.
所以艾丽西亚先去了她平时给菲利斯买衣服的那些店。

778
00:42:23.490 --> 00:42:27.990
And she was really concerned about Phyllis feeling comfortable in this outfit.
她非常担心菲利斯穿上这套衣服会觉得不自在。

779
00:42:28.270 --> 00:42:33.130
She shared that she had color palettes for all of our characters.
她说她为我们所有角色都设定了调色板。

780
00:42:33.170 --> 00:42:36.950
And she looked at the color palettes for Pam and Phyllis.
她查看了帕姆和菲利斯的调色板。

781
00:42:36.950 --> 00:42:39.830
And she saw that we had a few overlapping colors.
她发现我们有一些重叠的颜色。

782
00:42:40.120 --> 00:42:47.490
And our overlapping colors were mauve, mint, cocoa brown, navy, and purple.
我们重叠的颜色是淡紫色、薄荷绿、可可棕、海军蓝和紫色。

783
00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:53.930
I would dare say that purple was an overlapping color for the majority of the office.
我敢说，紫色是办公室里大多数人都有的重叠色。

784
00:42:53.930 --> 00:42:56.310
I think Alicia likes purple.
我觉得艾丽西亚喜欢紫色。

785
00:42:56.630 --> 00:42:59.210
Well, I had a purple breakdown of a whole scene.
嗯，我之前还做过一个关于紫色在整场戏中分布的详细分析。

786
00:42:59.570 --> 00:43:02.710
I think when we have Alicia on the podcast, we're going to ask her,
我想等艾丽西亚上我们的播客时，我们要问问她，

787
00:43:02.850 --> 00:43:04.090
what's your favorite color?
你最喜欢的颜色是什么？

788
00:43:04.390 --> 00:43:05.490
Let's see if she says purple.
看看她会不会说是紫色。

789
00:43:05.510 --> 00:43:06.550
I think she's going to say purple.
我觉得她会说是紫色。

790
00:43:06.550 --> 00:43:10.070
So she said the first item she found was the plaid shirt.
她说她找到的第一件单品是那件格子衬衫。

791
00:43:10.350 --> 00:43:12.850
And she thought that was a good place to start.
她觉得这是一个很好的起点。

792
00:43:13.090 --> 00:43:17.510
She said, also, our characters both tended to layer our clothes.
她说，我们的角色也都倾向于叠穿衣服。

793
00:43:18.750 --> 00:43:25.270
And she thought, though, that there needed to be something that wasn't too Phyllis or too Pam about it.
但她认为，这套衣服需要有一些既不太像菲利斯、也不太像帕姆的元素。

794
00:43:25.290 --> 00:43:29.450
So she thought the little sweater shrug was another good crossover item.
所以她觉得那件小针织开衫是另一个很好的折中选择。

795
00:43:29.650 --> 00:43:31.930
So that was her first choice of outfit.
这就是她最初选定的服装方案。

796
00:43:32.750 --> 00:43:34.910
And then she bought it in both of our sizes.
然后她买了我们两个尺码的衣服。

797
00:43:34.910 --> 00:43:38.990
And then she found two other outfits that she thought might work.
接着她又找了另外两套她觉得可能合适的衣服。

798
00:43:39.290 --> 00:43:42.870
Well, this is all happening at 9 p.m.
嗯，这一切发生的时候已经是晚上9点了，

799
00:43:43.150 --> 00:43:47.230
as the mall is closing the night before we had to shoot this.
就在我们拍摄前一晚商场快要关门的时候。

800
00:43:47.570 --> 00:43:48.710
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

801
00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:50.230
That's how little time she had.
她当时的时间就是这么紧。

802
00:43:50.330 --> 00:43:52.350
She's, like, sprinting through the mall.
她就像在商场里冲刺一样。

803
00:43:52.430 --> 00:43:52.750
Yes.
没错。

804
00:43:53.010 --> 00:43:55.710
So the next morning, Phyllis came in for her fitting.
第二天早上，菲利斯来试装了。

805
00:43:56.470 --> 00:43:59.810
And Alicia said the plaid shirt was the clear winner.
艾丽西亚说那件格子衬衫显然是最佳选择。

806
00:44:00.370 --> 00:44:01.890
I came in for my fitting.
我来试装了。

807
00:44:01.910 --> 00:44:03.130
I thought it was really cute.
我觉得它真的很可爱。

808
00:44:03.130 --> 00:44:05.570
They altered the top a little bit for me.
她们帮我稍微改了一下上衣。

809
00:44:05.710 --> 00:44:08.850
You might notice that my version is a little more fitted in the cheSt.
你们可能注意到了，我这件在胸部位置更合身一些。

810
00:44:09.370 --> 00:44:13.490
I will say, looking back, this is not a fashionable outfit.
我得说，回过头来看，这身打扮真不时尚。

811
00:44:14.390 --> 00:44:15.170
It is.
挺时尚的。

812
00:44:15.290 --> 00:44:15.970
It is not.
一点也不。

813
00:44:16.150 --> 00:44:16.830
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

814
00:44:16.950 --> 00:44:18.110
The plaid shirt is fine.
格子衬衫没问题。

815
00:44:18.250 --> 00:44:19.130
It's the sweater.
问题出在那件毛衣上。

816
00:44:19.870 --> 00:44:21.590
I don't know what you call that thing.
我不知道那玩意儿叫什么。

817
00:44:21.690 --> 00:44:22.470
It's not a shrug.
那不是小披肩。

818
00:44:22.630 --> 00:44:24.030
She called it a shrug.
她管它叫小披肩。

819
00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:25.310
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

820
00:44:25.510 --> 00:44:27.190
Just listen to the word shrug.
听听“小披肩”这个词。

821
00:44:27.750 --> 00:44:29.370
Is that something you want to wear?
那是你想穿的东西吗？

822
00:44:29.550 --> 00:44:29.850
Where?
哪儿？

823
00:44:30.350 --> 00:44:33.470
Listen, back then, those shrugs were a thing.
听着，那时候小披肩确实很流行。

824
00:44:33.870 --> 00:44:34.690
They were.
确实流行过。

825
00:44:34.930 --> 00:44:35.910
You can look it up.
你可以去查查。

826
00:44:36.150 --> 00:44:38.330
And capri pants were a thing.
那时候七分裤也很流行。

827
00:44:38.490 --> 00:44:38.890
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

828
00:44:38.890 --> 00:44:46.050
So, I think maybe this outfit has just not held up great over time, really.
所以我觉得，这身装扮经不起时间的考验，真的。

829
00:44:46.470 --> 00:44:52.610
But at the same time, Pam has never been a real fashion forward gal.
但话说回来，帕姆从来都不是那种走在时尚前沿的女孩。

830
00:44:52.850 --> 00:44:55.170
You know, she saw something on a mannequin.
你知道，她看到模特身上穿了什么。

831
00:44:55.430 --> 00:44:56.770
She tried it.
她就试了试。

832
00:44:56.770 --> 00:45:04.210
But I do like looking back, trying to imagine, like, how did Jim handle this back at the house
但我确实喜欢回想一下，试着想象吉姆在家里是怎么应对的，

833
00:45:04.210 --> 00:45:07.210
when she's like, what do you think?
当她问他：你觉得怎么样？

834
00:45:07.750 --> 00:45:10.130
Jim is like, it's great.
吉姆会说：很棒。

835
00:45:10.190 --> 00:45:11.870
It's different.
很特别。

836
00:45:12.270 --> 00:45:15.110
How did, what, have you had that moment with your husband?
你有过和你丈夫这样的时刻吗？

837
00:45:15.310 --> 00:45:15.730
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

838
00:45:16.070 --> 00:45:18.730
Jim wore a knit tie for years.
吉姆戴了好几年的针织领带。

839
00:45:19.170 --> 00:45:24.590
He also bought his parents' house that had a clown mounted to the wall, a clown painting.
他还买了他父母的房子，墙上挂着个小丑，一幅小丑画。

840
00:45:25.370 --> 00:45:29.030
I don't know that Jim has his finger on the pulse of fashion.
我不觉得吉姆对时尚有什么敏锐的触觉。

841
00:45:29.270 --> 00:45:30.350
I guess you're right.
我想你是对的。

842
00:45:30.710 --> 00:45:33.490
I think he probably thinks Pam looks cute and everything.
我觉得他可能觉得帕姆看起来很可爱之类的。

843
00:45:34.370 --> 00:45:34.570
Hmm.
嗯。

844
00:45:35.470 --> 00:45:35.830
Yeah.
是啊。

845
00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:40.150
Lee has tried that for me when I'm like, okay, what do you think of this outfit?
李也试过这样对我，当我问他：好吧，你觉得这身衣服怎么样？

846
00:45:40.330 --> 00:45:42.350
He'll say, I think you look beautiful and everything.
他会说：我觉得你看起来很漂亮之类的。

847
00:45:42.670 --> 00:45:46.510
I'll say, well, obviously, I'm not getting this outfit because if I looked good,
我会说：好吧，显然我不会买这身衣服，因为如果我穿起来好看，

848
00:45:46.570 --> 00:45:47.710
you'd just tell me I looked good.
你只会告诉我我看起来很好看。

849
00:45:47.810 --> 00:45:51.030
He'd be like, no, I'm telling you, I think you're beautiful and everything.
他会说：不，我是认真的，我觉得你很漂亮之类的。

850
00:45:51.150 --> 00:45:52.030
I think you're beautiful.
我觉得你很漂亮。

851
00:45:52.030 --> 00:45:52.930
I love you.
我爱你。

852
00:45:52.930 --> 00:45:54.970
And I'm like, okay, okay.
我就想，好吧，好吧。

853
00:45:55.330 --> 00:45:56.210
Take a picture of me.
给我拍张照。

854
00:45:56.210 --> 00:45:57.150
I'm going to send it to Angela.
我要发给安吉拉。

855
00:45:58.410 --> 00:45:59.730
I need a real opinion.
我需要一个真实的评价。

856
00:46:00.050 --> 00:46:00.270
This is true.
这是真的。

857
00:46:00.450 --> 00:46:04.250
I get, whenever Jenna has to buy an outfit for anything, four years.
每当珍娜需要为任何场合买衣服时，这持续了四年。

858
00:46:04.430 --> 00:46:07.150
This is like over a decade now.
这都超过十年了。

859
00:46:07.410 --> 00:46:11.410
I get a little photo shoot spread texted to me.
我都会收到她发来的一组照片。

860
00:46:11.470 --> 00:46:11.770
Yes.
没错。

861
00:46:11.990 --> 00:46:12.990
And you ask my thoughts.
而且你会问我的想法。

862
00:46:13.290 --> 00:46:15.330
What would you say if I sent you this outfit?
如果我发给你这套衣服，你会怎么说？

863
00:46:15.690 --> 00:46:18.550
I would say skip the purple shruggy thing.
我会说别穿那件紫色的短外套。

864
00:46:18.870 --> 00:46:19.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

865
00:46:19.290 --> 00:46:20.030
Keep the shirt.
留下那件衬衫。

866
00:46:20.510 --> 00:46:21.570
Khaki pants are fine.
卡其裤还可以。

867
00:46:21.890 --> 00:46:22.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

868
00:46:22.930 --> 00:46:23.230
Okay.
好吧。

869
00:46:23.230 --> 00:46:24.930
You know, given when this episode aired.
你知道，考虑到这一集播出的时间。

870
00:46:25.330 --> 00:46:25.570
Okay.
好吧。

871
00:46:25.970 --> 00:46:26.850
Fair enough.
说得也是。

872
00:46:27.410 --> 00:46:30.250
Well, Phyllis has a ton of sass in this episode.
菲利斯在这一集里真是太刻薄了。

873
00:46:30.530 --> 00:46:31.490
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

874
00:46:31.490 --> 00:46:34.150
She tells Pam that she looks like a trout.
她告诉帕姆说她看起来像条鳟鱼。

875
00:46:34.550 --> 00:46:37.210
She says, close your mouth, sweetie.
她说，把嘴闭上，亲爱的。

876
00:46:37.450 --> 00:46:38.530
You look like a trout.
你看起来像条鳟鱼。

877
00:46:38.530 --> 00:46:41.050
This is an epic insult.
这真是史诗级的侮辱。

878
00:46:41.310 --> 00:46:41.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

879
00:46:41.750 --> 00:46:44.090
I am telling you, that is like amazing.
我跟你说，这简直太绝了。

880
00:46:44.570 --> 00:46:49.630
Could you imagine saying to someone, you look like a trout?
你能想象对别人说，你看起来像条鳟鱼吗？

881
00:46:50.210 --> 00:46:50.610
No.
不能。

882
00:46:51.070 --> 00:46:57.810
I think it's like, you know how in your mind, you have like a fantasy argument with someone who
我觉得这就像，你知道你脑子里会和某人进行一场幻想中的争吵，那个人是

883
00:46:57.810 --> 00:47:01.530
you've always wanted to tell off, but maybe you're like me and you're not confrontational.
你一直想教训的人，但也许你像我一样，不善于对抗。

884
00:47:01.790 --> 00:47:02.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

885
00:47:02.070 --> 00:47:03.550
This is a fantasy moment.
这是一个幻想时刻。

886
00:47:03.850 --> 00:47:04.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

887
00:47:04.610 --> 00:47:05.630
Close your mouth, sweetie.
把嘴闭上，亲爱的。

888
00:47:05.870 --> 00:47:07.070
You look like a trout.
你看起来像条鳟鱼。

889
00:47:07.750 --> 00:47:13.410
This is going to take us to a scene where Angela is complaining to Toby because Oscar has worn sandals
接下来我们要看一个场景，安吉拉在向托比抱怨，因为奥斯卡穿了凉鞋

890
00:47:13.410 --> 00:47:14.850
and you can see his feet.
而且你能看到他的脚。

891
00:47:15.310 --> 00:47:16.830
Jenna, the scene was so much fun to do.
珍娜，拍这个场景太有趣了。

892
00:47:17.050 --> 00:47:18.850
I had so much fun yelling at Toby.
我冲托比大喊大叫，玩得太开心了。

893
00:47:21.170 --> 00:47:24.330
And as I exit, I say, excuse me.
当我离开时，我说，打扰一下。

894
00:47:24.390 --> 00:47:25.930
Oh, you're so educated, aren't you, Toby?
哦，你真是受过良好教育，不是吗，托比？

895
00:47:26.070 --> 00:47:27.950
So trained to deal with a hysterical woman.
真是训练有素，懂得如何应付歇斯底里的女人。

896
00:47:28.590 --> 00:47:30.810
I had an improvisation that made it in.
我有一个即兴发挥被保留了下来。

897
00:47:31.130 --> 00:47:33.930
I yelled, I don't want to look at his feet.
我大喊，我不想看他的脚。

898
00:47:34.390 --> 00:47:35.330
And that was improv.
那是即兴发挥。

899
00:47:35.730 --> 00:47:36.410
Very good.
非常好。

900
00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:37.190
Thank you.
谢谢。

901
00:47:37.770 --> 00:47:40.190
But you guys, let's think about this for a second.
但是各位，让我们仔细想一想。

902
00:47:40.610 --> 00:47:45.630
Do you really want to look at men's feet at work or on an airplane?
你们真的想在工作时或飞机上看到男人的脚吗？

903
00:47:46.010 --> 00:47:48.710
You guys that wear flip-flops on airplanes, I get it.
那些在飞机上穿人字拖的家伙，我懂你们的意思。

904
00:47:48.710 --> 00:47:49.710
Maybe it's your vacation.
