我简直不敢相信。

1057
00:55:34.850 --> 00:55:38.750
Yeah, I'm just sort of speechless at the gravity of that story and how it's amazing.
是啊，那个故事的沉重感和它的惊人之处让我简直无言以对。

1058
00:55:39.030 --> 00:55:41.590
I think we should take a break.
我想我们该休息一下了。

1059
00:55:41.730 --> 00:55:42.130
Yes.
好的。

1060
00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:46.390
And when we come back, we find out yet a new detail of Toby.
等我们回来，会发现关于托比的又一个新细节。

1061
00:55:46.730 --> 00:55:47.510
What is Toby?
托比到底是什么人？

1062
00:55:47.790 --> 00:55:48.750
Toby's like this onion.
托比就像个洋葱。

1063
00:55:48.930 --> 00:55:50.450
We're just peeling layers back about him.
我们只是在剥开关于他的层层外衣。

1064
00:56:01.620 --> 00:56:02.680
Snippet of a scene.
一段场景片段。

1065
00:56:02.860 --> 00:56:10.480
It's just a tiny moment where Toby is trying to get Oscar to take his socks, and he says
这只是个小插曲，托比试图让奥斯卡拿走他的袜子，他说

1066
00:56:10.480 --> 00:56:11.000
they're clean.
它们是干净的。

1067
00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:13.120
He was going to wear them to volleyball practice.
他本来打算穿着它们去参加排球训练的。

1068
00:56:13.720 --> 00:56:14.940
Who the heck is Toby?
托比到底是谁啊？

1069
00:56:15.480 --> 00:56:16.820
Who is this person?
这人是谁？

1070
00:56:17.560 --> 00:56:20.460
Was he in a weekly volleyball game?
他参加了每周一次的排球比赛吗？

1071
00:56:20.680 --> 00:56:22.280
Like, he plays adult volleyball?
你是说，他参加成人排球赛？

1072
00:56:22.280 --> 00:56:22.940
All right.
好吧。

1073
00:56:23.060 --> 00:56:26.600
We got some fan mail that had a few theories on this.
我们收到了一些粉丝来信，里面有几种关于此事的理论。

1074
00:56:27.040 --> 00:56:32.480
One of them being that, you know, it's going to be revealed in Company Picnic that Pam likes
其中之一是，你知道，在《公司野餐》那一集里会揭露帕姆喜欢

1075
00:56:32.480 --> 00:56:32.940
volleyball.
排球。

1076
00:56:33.320 --> 00:56:33.760
Oh.
哦。

1077
00:56:34.120 --> 00:56:36.920
Is he trying to get good at volleyball to impress Pam?
他是想通过练好排球来给帕姆留下好印象吗？

1078
00:56:36.920 --> 00:56:38.960
That is what people were saying.
大家都是这么说的。

1079
00:56:39.280 --> 00:56:39.940
That is so cute.
那太可爱了。

1080
00:56:39.960 --> 00:56:45.300
That this volleyball game is coming up, and maybe he wants to have something in common with Pam.
说是排球比赛快到了，也许他想和帕姆有共同话题。

1081
00:56:45.540 --> 00:56:46.680
Oh, I love that.
哦，我喜欢这个说法。

1082
00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:50.860
Well, Dwight's secret message is not received.
好吧，德怀特的秘密信息没传达到位。

1083
00:56:50.860 --> 00:56:57.580
So he is going to just tell everybody who is a salesperson who isn't Pam or Ryan go down to the warehouse.
所以他打算直接告诉除了帕姆和瑞安以外的所有销售人员去仓库。

1084
00:56:57.580 --> 00:56:59.600
I love the scene in the warehouse.
我喜欢仓库里的那个场景。

1085
00:56:59.860 --> 00:57:01.860
I thought it was such a great ensemble scene.
我觉得那是一个非常棒的群戏场景。

1086
00:57:02.080 --> 00:57:07.400
It reminded me of how when Michael has to lead a conference room scene and everyone keeps getting him off track.
它让我想起迈克尔主持会议室场景时，大家总是让他偏离主题的样子。

1087
00:57:07.980 --> 00:57:15.440
It was much longer than what you see in the actual episode, and I really wanted you guys to hear the rest of the scene.
它比你在正片里看到的要长得多，我真的很想让你们听听剩下的部分。

1088
00:57:16.720 --> 00:57:17.860
Thank you all for coming.
感谢大家的到来。

1089
00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:21.440
Now, please, everyone take a candle.
现在，请大家每人拿一支蜡烛。

1090
00:57:21.640 --> 00:57:22.560
We don't have time for candles.
我们没时间搞蜡烛了。

1091
00:57:22.800 --> 00:57:23.680
I think we're all in the bathroom.
我觉得我们都在洗手间里。

1092
00:57:24.500 --> 00:57:25.100
Skip the candles.
别管蜡烛了。

1093
00:57:26.180 --> 00:57:27.200
Let's cut to the chase.
我们开门见山吧。

1094
00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:28.600
How annoying is this, huh?
这有多烦人，嗯？

1095
00:57:29.160 --> 00:57:31.040
Do you mean what's going on today or this meeting?
你是说今天发生的事还是这个会议？

1096
00:57:31.340 --> 00:57:33.400
No, obviously what's happening at the meeting is not annoying.
不，显然会议本身并不烦人。

1097
00:57:33.540 --> 00:57:35.020
Only certain people in it are annoying.
只是里面某些人很烦人。

1098
00:57:35.260 --> 00:57:36.800
Can I take one of these candles home?
我可以带一支蜡烛回家吗？

1099
00:57:37.700 --> 00:57:42.380
Gentlemen, it's time to put our balls in the guillotine, as they say.
各位先生，正如他们所说，是时候把我们的蛋蛋放进断头台了。

1100
00:57:42.620 --> 00:57:44.060
Who has ever said that?
谁会这么说啊？

1101
00:57:44.060 --> 00:57:45.420
That's a regional expression.
那是地方方言。

1102
00:57:45.900 --> 00:57:49.320
I'm talking about going to Michael and telling him that we are ready to quit.
我是说去找迈克尔，告诉他我们准备辞职了。

1103
00:57:49.640 --> 00:57:50.540
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1104
00:57:50.720 --> 00:57:51.880
I don't know.
我不知道。

1105
00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:54.200
Yeah, Dwight, what if he calls our bluff?
是啊，德怀特，万一他看穿我们在虚张声势呢？

1106
00:57:54.440 --> 00:57:55.080
Then we are gone.
那我们就走人。

1107
00:57:55.640 --> 00:57:59.500
Because if we do nothing, then we fail, and failure is not an option.
因为如果我们什么都不做，那我们就失败了，而失败是不被允许的。

1108
00:57:59.860 --> 00:58:01.040
Well, hold on now.
等等，先别急。

1109
00:58:01.040 --> 00:58:02.180
Let's think this through.
让我们仔细考虑一下。

1110
00:58:02.660 --> 00:58:05.740
If we do nothing, at least we'll have our jobs.
如果我们什么都不做，至少我们还能保住工作。

1111
00:58:07.800 --> 00:58:10.600
If we do nothing, we fail, and failure is not an option.
如果我们什么都不做，我们就会失败，而失败是不被允许的。

1112
00:58:11.120 --> 00:58:13.000
Well, to be clear, it is an option.
好吧，说清楚点，失败是允许的。

1113
00:58:13.160 --> 00:58:13.980
Not in my book.
在我的字典里不是。

1114
00:58:14.540 --> 00:58:16.940
My book, the cover, is failure is not an option.
我的字典，封面就是“失败是不被允许的”。

1115
00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:18.260
It is an option.
它是允许的。

1116
00:58:18.420 --> 00:58:19.200
Not in my book.
在我的字典里不是。

1117
00:58:19.780 --> 00:58:20.260
Literally.
字面意义上。

1118
00:58:20.760 --> 00:58:20.810
What book?
什么字典？

1119
00:58:21.080 --> 00:58:21.540
What are you talking about?
你在说什么？

1120
00:58:21.540 --> 00:58:22.440
Did you write it?
那是你写的吗？

1121
00:58:23.340 --> 00:58:26.780
All day.
整天都在写。

1122
00:58:27.040 --> 00:58:30.640
Oh, that's when they would just let us keep talking and character.
哦，那是他们让我们保持角色设定继续交谈的时候。

1123
00:58:31.000 --> 00:58:31.480
Yes.
是的。

1124
00:58:31.640 --> 00:58:34.220
It's sort of like a long-form improv exercise.
这有点像是一种长篇即兴表演练习。

1125
00:58:34.900 --> 00:58:42.180
Well, while all this is happening in the warehouse, Pam, Ryan, and Michael are like best friends.
嗯，当仓库里发生这一切时，帕姆、瑞安和迈克尔就像是最好的朋友。

1126
00:58:42.500 --> 00:58:47.620
They're up in Michael's office, and they are giggling over this photo collage Michael has made.
他们待在迈克尔的办公室里，对着迈克尔制作的照片拼贴画咯咯直笑。

1127
00:58:47.620 --> 00:58:50.960
I mean, Ryan and Pam hated each other at Michael Scott Paper Company.
我是说，在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司时，瑞安和帕姆可是互相讨厌的。

1128
00:58:51.120 --> 00:58:55.060
And now they're just like, it's like they're old war buddies or something.
而现在他们看起来就像是老战友什么的。

1129
00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:56.540
I loved it.
我喜欢这样。

1130
00:58:56.640 --> 00:58:57.880
I loved this dynamic.
我喜欢这种互动关系。

1131
00:58:57.880 --> 00:59:01.180
We had a fan question from Adrian M.
我们收到了来自阿德里安·M的一位粉丝提问。

1132
00:59:01.460 --> 00:59:04.980
on the memory board that Michael makes.
关于迈克尔制作的记忆板。

1133
00:59:04.980 --> 00:59:06.500
When were the photos taken?
这些照片是什么时候拍的？

1134
00:59:07.100 --> 00:59:11.200
Was it done while you were filming the Michael Scott Paper Company episodes?
是在拍摄《迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司》那几集的时候拍的吗？

1135
00:59:12.160 --> 00:59:13.740
Yes, Adrian, they were.
是的，阿德里安，确实是。

1136
00:59:14.020 --> 00:59:21.860
We knew ahead of time that we were going to need these photos because Randy Cordray, he would get the scripts early.
我们提前就知道需要这些照片，因为兰迪·科德雷总是能提前拿到剧本。

1137
00:59:22.400 --> 00:59:29.400
So that he could anticipate sight gags and props and locations and all these things that go into planning an episode.
这样他就能预见到视觉笑话、道具、外景地以及所有筹备一集节目所需的东西。

1138
00:59:29.700 --> 00:59:32.800
So he knew that for this episode, we would need these pictures.
所以他知道这一集我们需要这些照片。

1139
00:59:33.020 --> 00:59:38.120
So while we were filming broke, we took all these pictures for the collage.
因此，在拍摄《破产》那一集时，我们拍了所有这些照片来做拼贴画。

1140
00:59:38.540 --> 00:59:43.380
A storyline is about to start that I loved so much, Jenna, and it is Jim and Creed.
有一条我非常喜欢的剧情线要开始了，珍娜，是关于吉姆和克里德的。

1141
00:59:43.620 --> 00:59:44.720
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1142
00:59:44.720 --> 00:59:52.700
I loved how, like, Creed is being so normal that it makes you more suspicious of him.
我喜欢克里德表现得如此正常，反而让你对他更加怀疑。

1143
00:59:53.480 --> 00:59:56.360
I loved just whenever Jim and Creed were in scenes together.
我就是喜欢吉姆和克里德在一起的任何场景。

1144
00:59:56.360 --> 01:00:01.680
And as you know, John Krasinski was always just, like, completely disintegrating into laughter.
如你所知，约翰·卡拉辛斯基总是会完全忍不住笑场。

1145
01:00:01.900 --> 01:00:03.620
Well, John loved doing scenes with Creed.
嗯，约翰很喜欢和克里德演对手戏。

1146
01:00:04.060 --> 01:00:09.540
So I called Creed because I was like, Creed, you have this hilarious storyline with Jim in this episode.
所以我给克里德打了电话，我说，克里德，你在这一集里和吉姆有一段超搞笑的剧情。

1147
01:00:09.540 --> 01:00:10.980
And I sort of reminded him of it.
我算是提醒了他一下。

1148
01:00:11.160 --> 01:00:14.540
I had the shooting draft, and we went through it together, Jenna.
我有拍摄底稿，我们一起过了一遍，珍娜。

1149
01:00:15.080 --> 01:00:15.520
Aww.
噢。

1150
01:00:15.840 --> 01:00:16.520
I know.
我知道。

1151
01:00:16.940 --> 01:00:21.680
And one of the things that cracked us up, it was a line that Creed loved, and it didn't make it in.
有一件事让我们笑得不行，那是Creed很喜欢的一句台词，但最后没用上。

1152
01:00:21.740 --> 01:00:22.800
I want to share it with you.
我想和你们分享一下。

1153
01:00:23.860 --> 01:00:31.280
So the scene starts that Creed is in the corner, and in the shooting draft, Jim gets a soda, and Creed says,
场景开始时Creed在角落里，在拍摄剧本中，Jim去拿汽水，Creed说，

1154
01:00:31.480 --> 01:00:33.020
you're going to be happy with that.
你会对那个满意的。

1155
01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:33.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1156
01:00:34.240 --> 01:00:35.500
And Jim says, hi.
Jim说，嗨。

1157
01:00:35.900 --> 01:00:38.320
And then Creed says, I come here to take a break.
然后Creed说，我来这儿是为了休息一下。

1158
01:00:38.460 --> 01:00:39.480
And Jim says, yeah.
Jim说，是啊。

1159
01:00:39.980 --> 01:00:41.420
Here's the line that got cut.
这就是被删掉的那句台词。

1160
01:00:41.960 --> 01:00:43.540
Creed says, the restroom.
Creed说，洗手间。

1161
01:00:43.540 --> 01:00:44.940
That's what I call it.
我是这么叫它的。

1162
01:00:46.920 --> 01:00:49.760
Creed calls the break room the restroom.
Creed把休息室叫作洗手间。

1163
01:00:50.700 --> 01:00:52.580
And then the rest is scripted.
剩下的部分就是剧本里的内容了。

1164
01:00:52.840 --> 01:00:57.540
Let's talk about this storyline, because eventually Creed is going to suggest that they play a game.
我们来聊聊这个故事线，因为最终Creed会建议他们玩个游戏。

1165
01:00:58.080 --> 01:00:58.600
Yes.
没错。

1166
01:00:58.800 --> 01:01:00.680
And that game is going to be chess.
那个游戏是国际象棋。

1167
01:01:00.960 --> 01:01:01.440
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1168
01:01:01.440 --> 01:01:06.420
And not only that, Creed is a very good chess player.
不仅如此，Creed还是个非常厉害的棋手。

1169
01:01:06.780 --> 01:01:07.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1170
01:01:07.520 --> 01:01:12.300
Well, I texted with John Krasinski about this because I wanted to know, is John a good chess player?
我为此给John Krasinski发了短信，因为我想知道，John的棋艺好吗？

1171
01:01:12.740 --> 01:01:14.500
Because I knew you were reaching out to Creed.
因为我知道你在联系Creed。

1172
01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:16.160
So I was like, I'll get John's side of this.
所以我当时想，我也得听听John那边的说法。

1173
01:01:16.740 --> 01:01:19.660
John said he knows how to play chess, but very poorly.
John说他会下国际象棋，但下得很烂。

1174
01:01:19.660 --> 01:01:21.340
Well, this is what Creed said.
嗯，Creed是这么说的。

1175
01:01:21.500 --> 01:01:24.140
Creed said, yes, I can play chess.
Creed说，是的，我会下国际象棋。

1176
01:01:24.300 --> 01:01:27.480
I'm not an aficionado, but I have basic skills.
我算不上什么行家，但我有基本功。

1177
01:01:27.480 --> 01:01:31.520
And he said he's actually looking forward to playing chess with his granddaughters.
他还说他其实很期待和孙女们一起下棋。

1178
01:01:31.920 --> 01:01:32.400
Oh.
哦。

1179
01:01:32.800 --> 01:01:34.400
He wants to share it with them.
他想和她们分享这个游戏。

1180
01:01:34.600 --> 01:01:35.320
Oh, you know what?
哦，你知道吗？

1181
01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:37.660
Lee's dad plays chess with my son.
Lee的爸爸会和我儿子下棋。

1182
01:01:37.880 --> 01:01:42.380
And it warms my heart every time I look over and see them playing chess.
每次我转头看到他们下棋，心里都暖暖的。

1183
01:01:42.500 --> 01:01:44.380
It's like his thing he does with his grandpa.
那是他和爷爷之间专属的活动。

1184
01:01:44.800 --> 01:01:45.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1185
01:01:45.080 --> 01:01:51.460
And then what's so fantastic is this chess runner ends with Jim's talking head that says,
最棒的是，这个下棋的桥段以Jim的采访镜头结尾，他说，

1186
01:01:51.660 --> 01:01:57.140
I'm just hiding out until all this stuff blows over with Creed playing chess at work.
我只是在躲着，直到Creed在办公室下棋这事儿平息下来。

1187
01:01:57.340 --> 01:01:58.180
He's winning.
他赢了。

1188
01:01:58.440 --> 01:02:00.340
I feel like I'm describing a dream I had.
我感觉自己像是在描述我做过的一个梦。

1189
01:02:00.480 --> 01:02:01.980
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1190
01:02:03.120 --> 01:02:07.700
So listen, when the gang comes back from down in the warehouse,
听着，当大家从仓库回来的时候，

1191
01:02:08.340 --> 01:02:11.320
Michael, Pam, and Ryan are like, where have you been?
Michael、Pam和Ryan问，你们去哪儿了？

1192
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:14.500
And they claim that they've been at lunch.
他们声称自己去吃午饭了。

1193
01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:18.120
And we're like, it's very early in the morning.
我们说，现在才大清早呢。

1194
01:02:18.320 --> 01:02:20.300
What all did you have for lunch?
你们午饭到底吃了什么？

1195
01:02:20.660 --> 01:02:22.280
Because they're trying to trap them.
因为他们想套出他们的话。

1196
01:02:22.760 --> 01:02:24.600
Andy very quickly shares this.
Andy很快就分享了这些。

1197
01:02:24.980 --> 01:02:27.160
I had a salmon salad with water, no ice.
我吃了三文鱼沙拉配水，不加冰。

1198
01:02:27.280 --> 01:02:29.300
I was going to get a soda, but the waiter talked me out of it.
我本来想点汽水，但服务员劝我别喝。

1199
01:02:29.500 --> 01:02:30.100
Her name was Flo.
她叫Flo。

1200
01:02:30.240 --> 01:02:30.900
She had black hair.
她留着黑头发。

1201
01:02:33.200 --> 01:02:36.820
And immediately, this is like the art of lying, okay?
立刻，这就像是撒谎的艺术，明白吗？

1202
01:02:37.200 --> 01:02:42.380
Like he thinks by sharing a ton of details that that's going to make him seem normal.
他以为分享一大堆细节就能让自己看起来很正常。

1203
01:02:42.380 --> 01:02:47.060
But let me tell you, whenever someone gives me an answer like this, I'm like, suspect.
但我告诉你，每当有人给我这样的回答时，我都会觉得很可疑。

1204
01:02:47.600 --> 01:02:52.960
Yeah, you want to have the detail, but you don't just lay it all out at the top in one big blob.
没错，你是想提供细节，但不能一开始就一股脑儿全倒出来。

1205
01:02:53.260 --> 01:02:53.560
No.
没错。

1206
01:02:53.940 --> 01:02:57.980
Michael, Pam, and Ryan are like, oh, well, if you guys, you know, went out to lunch,
迈克尔、帕姆和瑞安就像是，哦，好吧，如果你们，你知道，出去吃午饭了，

1207
01:02:58.120 --> 01:03:00.060
then I guess we can eat what's in the fridge here.
那我想我们就可以吃冰箱里的东西了。

1208
01:03:00.060 --> 01:03:04.900
Yes, and then the three of us go in the fridge, and we start eating everybody's lunches.
是的，然后我们三个就去翻冰箱，开始吃大家的午餐。

1209
01:03:05.040 --> 01:03:07.160
Please watch this in the bloopers, you guys.
大家一定要去看花絮，真的。

1210
01:03:07.280 --> 01:03:08.560
Well, I remember it.
嗯，我记得。

1211
01:03:09.100 --> 01:03:13.980
Steve took a huge bite out of a cold salmon filet.
史蒂夫咬了一大口冷三文鱼片。

1212
01:03:14.240 --> 01:03:17.020
You're shoveling potato salad in your mouth.
你当时正往嘴里猛塞土豆沙拉。

1213
01:03:17.140 --> 01:03:18.900
It was egg salad, lady.
那是蛋沙拉，女士。

1214
01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:19.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1215
01:03:19.740 --> 01:03:20.040
Egg salad.
蛋沙拉。

1216
01:03:20.280 --> 01:03:20.500
Gross.
真恶心。

1217
01:03:20.820 --> 01:03:23.040
And people asked, was it really egg salad?
有人问，那真的是蛋沙拉吗？

1218
01:03:23.220 --> 01:03:23.860
It was.
确实是。

1219
01:03:23.980 --> 01:03:25.580
Like, it was making us laugh.
当时我们都笑喷了。

1220
01:03:25.580 --> 01:03:32.100
You laughed so hard with a mouthful of egg salad that, like, there was, like, egg salad spittle.
你笑得太厉害，嘴里塞满蛋沙拉，甚至喷出了蛋沙拉碎屑。

1221
01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:33.040
It was so gross.
太恶心了。

1222
01:03:33.040 --> 01:03:33.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1223
01:03:34.120 --> 01:03:36.880
I mean, I remember it like it was yesterday.
我的意思是，我记得就像昨天发生的一样。

1224
01:03:37.300 --> 01:03:40.140
Well, we got a fan catch from Nikki S.
嗯，我们收到了一位粉丝尼基·S的提问，

1225
01:03:40.520 --> 01:03:41.580
about all this food.
关于这些食物的。

1226
01:03:41.780 --> 01:03:46.740
She says, when Michael is taking the sales staff's lunches out of the fridge,
她说，当迈克尔从冰箱里拿走销售人员的午餐时，

1227
01:03:46.900 --> 01:03:52.740
he takes a green-wrapped sandwich, and it's from a gas station chain called Sheets.
他拿了一个绿色包装的三明治，那是来自一家叫Sheets的加油站连锁店。

1228
01:03:52.740 --> 01:04:00.540
They are known for their food, commonly called MTO, which stands for made-to-order.
他们以食物闻名，通常被称为MTO，意思是按需定制。

1229
01:04:00.840 --> 01:04:08.540
So I looked it up, and there is this string of gas stations called Sheets in the area,
所以我查了一下，该地区确实有一连串叫Sheets的加油站，

1230
01:04:08.540 --> 01:04:12.160
and they make made-to-order food.
他们确实提供按需定制的食物。

1231
01:04:12.500 --> 01:04:13.800
Here's their commercial.
这是他们的广告。

1232
01:04:14.300 --> 01:04:16.020
I am starving.
我饿坏了。

1233
01:04:16.780 --> 01:04:17.620
Well, stop at Sheets.
去Sheets停一下吧。

1234
01:04:17.860 --> 01:04:19.520
You can't get good food at a gas station.
你不可能在加油站买到好吃的。

1235
01:04:21.560 --> 01:04:22.060
Really?
真的吗？

1236
01:04:22.060 --> 01:04:23.360
You couldn't have just agreed.
你就不能附和一下吗？

1237
01:04:23.760 --> 01:04:26.440
See, so in this moment, they've turned into donkeys.
你看，就在这一刻，他们变成了驴子。

1238
01:04:26.680 --> 01:04:30.160
You know what that does to you and me.
你知道那对你我意味着什么。

1239
01:04:30.940 --> 01:04:31.800
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1240
01:04:32.540 --> 01:04:32.980
Yep.
没错。

1241
01:04:33.260 --> 01:04:34.760
It makes an ass of you and me.
那会让你我变成蠢驴（ass）。

1242
01:04:35.540 --> 01:04:36.040
See?
看到了吗？

1243
01:04:36.240 --> 01:04:39.900
Don't assume you can't get fresh-made-to-order food at a gas station.
别以为你在加油站买不到新鲜的定制食品。

1244
01:04:41.040 --> 01:04:41.540
Sheets.
Sheets。

1245
01:04:42.480 --> 01:04:43.720
Feel the love.
感受这份爱。

1246
01:04:44.440 --> 01:04:44.680
Yeah.
没错。

1247
01:04:45.020 --> 01:04:46.380
Ding, dong, ding, dong, ding.
叮，咚，叮，咚，叮。

1248
01:04:46.380 --> 01:04:48.100
So here's...
所以这是……

1249
01:04:48.100 --> 01:04:49.220
What is that ad?
那是什么广告？

1250
01:04:49.600 --> 01:04:51.120
What is happening in that ad?
那广告里到底在演什么？

1251
01:04:51.120 --> 01:04:53.220
It's two people driving in a car, and they want some food.
有两个人开车在路上，他们想吃点东西。

1252
01:04:53.220 --> 01:04:57.780
And as soon as he assumes that you can't get made-to-order food at a gas station,
而一旦他认定你在加油站买不到现做的食物，

1253
01:04:58.040 --> 01:04:59.860
they turn into asses.
他们就变成了驴。

1254
01:05:00.360 --> 01:05:00.880
Oh.
噢。

1255
01:05:00.880 --> 01:05:01.900
And they start hee-hawing.
然后他们开始学驴叫。

1256
01:05:02.680 --> 01:05:06.600
But here's the thing that got me that I was thinking.
但有一件事让我一直在思考。

1257
01:05:06.900 --> 01:05:11.140
Do you remember in the injury when Michael wants some yams?
你还记得在《受伤》那一集里，迈克尔想吃山药吗？

1258
01:05:11.740 --> 01:05:12.240
Yeah.
记得。

1259
01:05:12.900 --> 01:05:15.540
Ryan says you can't get yams at a gas station?
瑞安说你在加油站买不到山药？

1260
01:05:15.880 --> 01:05:16.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1261
01:05:16.860 --> 01:05:19.840
I just wonder, does Sheets sell yams?
我只是在想，Sheets加油站卖山药吗？

1262
01:05:20.060 --> 01:05:21.700
Can I get a yam on my sandwich?
我的三明治里能加山药吗？

1263
01:05:22.040 --> 01:05:24.060
I looked at their menus.
我查了他们的菜单。

1264
01:05:24.060 --> 01:05:27.820
It seems like each location sometimes has slightly different iteMs.
看起来每个分店的商品有时会略有不同。

1265
01:05:27.820 --> 01:05:29.660
I could not find one that had yaMs.
我没找到哪家店有卖山药。

1266
01:05:29.700 --> 01:05:31.800
So I guess Ryan is still right.
所以我猜瑞安还是对的。

1267
01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:37.360
But Sheets, I think you should consider, I don't know, for all the office fans out there,
不过Sheets，我觉得你们应该考虑一下，我不知道，为了所有的《办公室》剧迷们，

1268
01:05:37.360 --> 01:05:41.060
if you started selling yams at your gas station, it might be a hit.
如果你们开始在加油站卖山药，可能会大受欢迎。

1269
01:05:41.280 --> 01:05:42.300
Maybe it's a holiday item.
也许可以作为节日限定商品。

1270
01:05:42.400 --> 01:05:43.320
Yeah, it's a holiday item.
没错，作为节日限定商品。

1271
01:05:43.500 --> 01:05:44.920
I have a question for Sheets.
我有个问题想问Sheets。

1272
01:05:45.060 --> 01:05:46.260
Is that bread for real?
那面包是真的吗？

1273
01:05:46.520 --> 01:05:50.580
Because that bread was like the size of a Buick.
因为那面包简直有别克车那么大。

1274
01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:51.380
I don't know.
我不知道。

1275
01:05:52.100 --> 01:05:54.420
It's seriously, that bread was the size of Steve's head.
说真的，那面包有史蒂夫的头那么大。

1276
01:05:54.800 --> 01:05:58.420
Here's an interesting tidbit that Brent shared in the DVD commentary.
这里有个布伦特在DVD评论音轨中分享的有趣花絮。

1277
01:05:58.420 --> 01:06:07.020
This entire third act was written in a breakout pod of writers of Mindy, BJ, Gene, and Lee in about 12 hours.
整个第三幕是由明迪、BJ、吉恩和李在一个临时小组里花了大约12小时写出来的。

1278
01:06:07.260 --> 01:06:07.780
Wow.
哇。

1279
01:06:07.960 --> 01:06:08.960
Entire third act.
整个第三幕。

1280
01:06:09.140 --> 01:06:15.660
I remember Brent sharing with us, and Alicia supports this, that this whole script came down to the wire.
我记得布伦特和我们分享过，艾丽西亚也证实了这一点，整个剧本当时写得非常紧迫。

1281
01:06:15.860 --> 01:06:18.380
That like, this is the end of the season.
就像是，这已经是季终集了。

1282
01:06:18.700 --> 01:06:20.200
They're backed up.
他们积压了很多工作。

1283
01:06:20.360 --> 01:06:21.980
They're running out of time.
时间快不够了。

1284
01:06:22.220 --> 01:06:23.360
We're on fumes.
我们已经精疲力竭了。

1285
01:06:23.360 --> 01:06:24.240
We are.
确实是。

1286
01:06:24.500 --> 01:06:29.920
Randy noted that this whole episode takes place just at Dunder Mifflin,
兰迪提到这一整集都发生在邓德·米夫林公司内部，

1287
01:06:30.120 --> 01:06:40.020
and that the production had requested that because they were getting ready for our big 100th episode season finale company picnic.
制作组之所以提出这个要求，是因为他们当时正在为第100集季终集——公司野餐做准备。

1288
01:06:40.020 --> 01:06:44.480
They were prepping, and he said, we just couldn't afford to be going on location.
他们正在筹备，他说，我们实在负担不起外景拍摄的开销。

1289
01:06:44.500 --> 01:06:48.860
We needed an episode that happened right on our set.
我们需要一集完全在摄影棚内完成的剧集。

1290
01:06:48.980 --> 01:06:52.960
So maybe that contributed, too, to some of these rewrites at the end.
所以这可能也促成了最后阶段的一些剧本重写。

1291
01:06:53.360 --> 01:07:00.080
I also want to give a shout-out to, you know, our unsung hero a little bit, Phil Shea, who every week had to do so much.
我还想特别感谢一下我们的一位无名英雄，菲尔·谢，他每周都要处理大量繁杂的工作。

1292
01:07:00.460 --> 01:07:08.780
If you go to deleted scenes, there's a scene where Jim is welcoming Pam to the desk pod of Jim and Dwight and Pam now.
如果你去看删减片段，会发现有一个场景是吉姆欢迎帕姆加入他和德怀特、帕姆现在的办公区。

1293
01:07:09.060 --> 01:07:15.720
And he gives her this little island, and on the island, it's Jim and Pam and Dwight.
他给了她这个小岛模型，岛上有吉姆、帕姆和德怀特。

1294
01:07:16.020 --> 01:07:16.540
Okay.
好吧。

1295
01:07:16.900 --> 01:07:17.140
Okay?
是吗？

1296
01:07:17.140 --> 01:07:18.580
It's like a little figurine.
就像一个小雕像。

1297
01:07:18.960 --> 01:07:20.680
Why do I not have this item?
为什么我没有这个东西？

1298
01:07:20.880 --> 01:07:22.140
You should own this item.
你应该拥有这个东西的。

1299
01:07:22.140 --> 01:07:27.780
In the script, it was supposed to be Jim, Pam, and Dwight, and deleted scenes, it's sort of like a makeshift of that.
剧本里原本设定的是吉姆、帕姆和德怀特，在删减片段里，那看起来像是个临时拼凑的版本。

1300
01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:32.000
But I guess Phil Shea spent tons of time getting this thing made.
但我猜菲尔·谢花了很多时间才把这东西做出来。

1301
01:07:32.200 --> 01:07:32.840
Of course.
当然。

1302
01:07:32.860 --> 01:07:33.800
And it didn't even make it in.
而且它甚至都没能入选。

1303
01:07:33.960 --> 01:07:34.240
Yeah.
没错。

1304
01:07:34.540 --> 01:07:41.320
Well, now we're coming up to a scene that is very famous as well, perhaps as famous as our chilly cold open.
好了，现在我们要讲到一个非常著名的场景，可能和我们那个冷开场一样出名。

1305
01:07:41.620 --> 01:07:42.340
For sure.
确实。

1306
01:07:42.340 --> 01:07:47.540
I mean, I've seen people do this scene as a Halloween costume.
我是说，我见过有人把这个场景当成万圣节装扮。

1307
01:07:48.080 --> 01:07:49.300
So many people.
好多人。

1308
01:07:49.660 --> 01:07:56.140
It's the scene where Toby has to confront Meredith about her casual outfit, saying that it's a bit revealing.
就是托比不得不找梅雷迪思谈话，说她的休闲装有点暴露的那个场景。

1309
01:07:56.220 --> 01:08:00.200
So when she tugs on her skirt, it flashes her top.
所以当她拉裙子的时候，上面就走光了。

1310
01:08:00.200 --> 01:08:03.220
When she pulls it back up, then it flashes the bottom.
当她把裙子拉回去的时候，下面又走光了。

1311
01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:05.020
It's a lot.
真是没眼看。

1312
01:08:05.280 --> 01:08:10.260
It has two standout famous lines that are quoted quite a bit to Kate Flannery.
这一幕有两句非常经典的台词，凯特·弗兰纳里经常被人引用。

1313
01:08:10.560 --> 01:08:12.140
Meredith, your boob is out.
梅雷迪思，你胸部露出来了。

1314
01:08:12.700 --> 01:08:15.100
And, damn it, Meredith, where are your panties?
还有，该死，梅雷迪思，你的内裤呢？

1315
01:08:15.860 --> 01:08:20.600
Well, when we talked to Brent Forrester about this episode, he told us this.
嗯，当我们和布伦特·福雷斯特聊到这一集时，他告诉了我们这些。

1316
01:08:20.820 --> 01:08:30.620
He said when he joined the writing staff of The Office in Season 3, he noticed that the writers were sometimes having a hard time writing for the character of Meredith,
他说当他在第三季加入《办公室》编剧组时，他注意到编剧们有时很难为梅雷迪思这个角色写剧本，

1317
01:08:30.920 --> 01:08:32.640
who he personally loved.
而他个人非常喜欢这个角色。

1318
01:08:32.900 --> 01:08:39.760
And he said everyone knew Kate Flannery was really funny, but they just hadn't cracked the code of this character.
他说大家都知道凯特·弗兰纳里很有趣，但他们就是没能参透这个角色的精髓。

1319
01:08:40.400 --> 01:08:44.360
Brent shared that one day he was at lunch, and he happened to be sitting next to Kate.
布伦特分享说，有一天他吃午饭时，正好坐在凯特旁边。

1320
01:08:44.360 --> 01:08:48.200
And so he just asked her, Kate, what makes you funny?
于是他就问她，凯特，你为什么这么有趣？

1321
01:08:48.440 --> 01:08:54.800
And apparently, Kate said something to the effect of, Brent, I'm the daughter of an old Irish bar owner.
显然，凯特当时大概是这么说的，布伦特，我是个老爱尔兰酒吧老板的女儿。

1322
01:08:54.980 --> 01:08:57.180
My comfort zone is loud and filthy.
我的舒适区就是吵闹和粗俗。

1323
01:08:57.740 --> 01:09:04.520
So he went back to the writers, and he told them this, and he said it revolutionized the writing for Meredith.
于是他回到编剧组，把这些告诉了大家，他说这彻底改变了梅雷迪思的剧本创作。

1324
01:09:04.520 --> 01:09:10.340
He got credited with cracking the code, and he was like, all I did was just ask the actress.
他被认为是参透了角色精髓的人，但他却说，我只是问了问演员而已。

1325
01:09:10.680 --> 01:09:12.380
He said it was actually a good lesson.
他说这其实是个很好的教训。

1326
01:09:12.380 --> 01:09:14.120
Like, go ask the actress.
比如，去问问演员。

1327
01:09:14.360 --> 01:09:15.700
Like, what are you really good at?
比如，你真正擅长的是什么？

1328
01:09:15.780 --> 01:09:16.720
What do you like to do?
你喜欢做什么？

1329
01:09:17.080 --> 01:09:17.960
What's your thing?
你的拿手好戏是什么？

1330
01:09:18.140 --> 01:09:20.180
And then the writer's room can lean into that.
然后编剧室就可以顺着这个方向去写。

1331
01:09:20.320 --> 01:09:22.340
And you mentioned this to Kate, right?
你跟凯特提过这事，对吧？

1332
01:09:22.580 --> 01:09:23.120
I did.
提过。

1333
01:09:23.140 --> 01:09:28.840
I was talking to Kate on the phone this week, and I said, Kate, we are coming up on Casual Friday.
这周我和凯特通电话时，我说，凯特，我们要讲到“休闲星期五”那一集了。

1334
01:09:29.180 --> 01:09:32.480
Also, you guys, when we're recording this, Halloween has just happened.
另外，各位，我们录制这一集的时候，万圣节刚过。

1335
01:09:33.040 --> 01:09:39.580
Kate is constantly tagged in photos of people dressed as Meredith in this purple dress.
凯特经常被人在照片里艾特，照片里的人都穿着梅雷迪思那件紫色裙子。

1336
01:09:39.580 --> 01:09:39.840
Yes.
没错。

1337
01:09:40.120 --> 01:09:42.080
With sort of a pixelated boob.
还带着那种打码的胸部效果。

1338
01:09:42.200 --> 01:09:42.580
Yes.
是的。

1339
01:09:42.780 --> 01:09:43.080
You know?
你知道吧？

1340
01:09:43.220 --> 01:09:43.680
I've seen them.
我见过那些照片。

1341
01:09:43.900 --> 01:09:44.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1342
01:09:44.580 --> 01:09:48.380
So I asked Kate about this scene, and here's what she had to share.
所以我问了凯特关于这个场景的事，以下是她的分享。

1343
01:09:48.380 --> 01:09:51.020
Hey, Office Lady Podcast fans.
嘿，《办公室女士》播客的粉丝们。

1344
01:09:51.180 --> 01:09:59.560
I have to tell you, when we did the table read, I knew exactly how well this was going to pull.
我必须告诉你们，当我们进行剧本围读时，我就确切地知道这一幕会产生多好的效果。

1345
01:09:59.640 --> 01:10:07.640
It was so well written, the scene where Toby tells Meredith to pull up her dress.
托比让梅雷迪思拉好裙子的那场戏写得太棒了。

1346
01:10:08.540 --> 01:10:16.540
It was just brilliantly written, and kind of like jumping out of an airplane whenever I'm topless or more.
写得真是绝妙，而且每当我需要半裸或更暴露时，就感觉像从飞机上跳下来一样。

1347
01:10:16.880 --> 01:10:17.360
Yeah.
没错。

1348
01:10:17.620 --> 01:10:18.740
